# Leaks of other libraries, held for the process's life, which
# LeakSanitizer reports in a sanitized test. Nothing of ours is in these
# frames.
#
# ALSA's library keeps its parsed configuration for the process's life;
# a test that opens a device on a machine with ALSA reports it as leaked
# (D401). Maul Audio loads the library at run time and unloads it, so its
# frames are often unnamed by the time LeakSanitizer reports; the calls
# into it are named by Maul Audio's own ALSA files instead (D403).
leak:libasound
leak:maul-audio/src/alsa_
# An OpenXR runtime keeps what it parsed of an application's suggested
# bindings (Monado's client library, 1 byte, D596). The loader unloads the
# runtime as the instance ends, so the runtime's frames are unnamed; the
# loader's entry point into it is named instead.
leak:xrSuggestInteractionProfileBindings
